message.content:
{"diagnosis": "Loopback send 0xa5 never results in recv_buf_valid, trace ends in uart timeout with no byte received. recv_state stays at 0 instead of advancing when start-bit (!ser_rx) is seen, so recv_divcnt is continually cleared and state 1 is never entered. Root cause in excerpt is line 80 assigning recv_state <= 0 to itself instead of recv_state <= 1.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -77,6 +77,6 @@
 			case (recv_state)
 				0: begin
 					if (!ser_rx)
-						recv_state <= 0;
+						recv_state <= 1;
 					recv_divcnt <= 0;
 				end
", "expected": "tohost: PASS loopback 0xa5 received, no uart timeout"}

